  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "PTR-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Independent vertex averaging preserves the period of a full cycle",
      "anchor": "inputs-period-vertices",
      "statement": "For an invariant homogeneous m-cocycle F and a finite bar m-cycle z, the evaluation at a fixed basepoint equals the signed sum of expectations obtained by replacing each simplex vertex h_j·I by h_j·Y_j with independent variables of the same law.",
      "hypotheses": "m=k+1≥1. F is invariant under the acting arithmetic group and its alternating face coboundary vanishes. All mixed configurations of fixed and averaged vertices are integrable. The probability in the selected application is normalized additive Haar on a compact ball B within the cone of positive definite Hermitian matrices, of strictly positive finite volume.",
      "definitions": [
        "The h_j are the successive partial products of a bar symbol and h₀=1.",
        "Give each point in H×{false,true} a group coordinate and a mark indicating whether to use the fixed basepoint or an independently sampled point.",
        "The marked cocycle is invariant because the original one is invariant. Deleting one coordinate of a product of identical probability laws leaves the product for the other coordinates."
      ],
