    {
      "id": "PTR-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Moving one simplex vertex bounds its density, and arithmetic discreteness bounds the overlap",
      "anchor": "inputs-period-density",
      "statement": "For each fixed arithmetic cycle z there is a finite C_z, chosen before the form, with |⟨ω,z⟩|≤C_z‖fr ω‖₂ on the finite-volume special-linear fundamental domain.",
      "hypotheses": "The local theorem takes a number field, N≥1, m≥1, and a fixed arithmetic cycle. The form is continuous on the cone, its simplex cochain is closed, it is invariant under GL_N(𝒪_L) and all archimedean central scalars, and its moving-frame squared norm is integrable on the stated fundamental domain.",
      "definitions": [
        "For τ in the standard m-simplex one coordinate τ_i is at least 1/(m+1). A_i is an invertible linear map on the real d-dimensional ambient vector space.",
        "With the other variables fixed, y_i↦τ_i A_i y_i+c has |det|=τ_i^d|det A_i|. The uniform conditional density bound is (m+1)^d/(vol(B)|det A_i|).",
        "K is the compact set of the possible convex combinations, K′ the compact set in the special-linear group supplied by the scalar-invariant unfolding estimate. f(x)=‖fr ω(x)‖. M=|Λ∩K′(K′)⁻¹|.",
        "In the written local bound a bar symbol contributes max(C₁,0) C₂ M √μ(D). C₁ comes from the simplex estimate, C₂ from compact unfolding. Sum these constants with absolute bar coefficients."
      ],
