    {
      "id": "PTR-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The same local constant bounds every Hecke-iterated period",
      "anchor": "inputs-period-rate",
      "statement": "For a good arithmetic and central invariant mean-zero remainder with L² moving coefficients and for each fixed cycle z, every iterate j satisfies |⟨H^jω₀,z⟩|≤|C_z|√(K_basis S₀)(3/5)^j.",
      "hypotheses": "The field is totally complex, N≥3 and π is a prime element with Norm((π))≥25. For each tangent tuple the coefficient satisfies the mean-zero, integrability and invariance requirements Lz. The selected mean-zero remainder ω′−ω̄ satisfies these conditions. Each comparison fixes the cycle z, matrix size, fundamental domain and starting form; the final upper constant is uniform in j.",
      "definitions": [
